      keyIdeas: [
        { en: "The stones in Estonia's fields were left by the ice, but the old legends say giants threw them." },
        { en: "A legend explains why a real place nearby is as it is; a fairy tale happens far away." },
        { en: "Legends have been collected for over a hundred and fifty years, and the pages are kept in the folklore archive in Tartu." },
        { en: "The best-known giant is Kalevipoeg, and places all over Estonia are linked to him." },
        { en: "In legends a lake can move away if people treat it badly: the stories are about how to treat nature." },
        { en: "Many places have a legend of a village sunk for its greed or pride, with a bell heard under the water." },
        { en: "Almost every village had a sacred grove where trees could not be cut, and some are protected by law today." },
        { en: "Legends did not happen as told, but most hold a grain of truth, a memory of something real." },
        { en: "New legends still appear: urban legends, spread online, about today's fears." },
        { en: "Legends matter because they tie people to places, keep old words alive and are good stories." },
      ],
